course: dictionary
lesson: 10360
title: Trappist: monks, silence and a star
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: A Trappist is a Catholic monk or nun who belongs to a strict order, the Cistercians of the Strict Observance. They pray, work hard and keep long periods of silence. «Trappist silence» is a phrase for keeping very quiet.
explain: Trappist can also be an adjective, so it describes things connected with this order: a «Trappist monastery» is a monastery where these monks live. Trappist beer and Trappist cheese are made in, or under the control of, Trappist monasteries.
explain: Use the context to decide which meaning fits. If the sentence talks about prayer, silence, farming or a monastery, Trappist means the monks. If it talks about a star, the word is being used as a name, so check the clues around it before you decide.
fact: A Trappist is a Catholic monk or nun of a strict order.
fact: Trappist monks pray several times a day and support themselves by farming, baking or brewing.
fact: Trappist monasteries include Mount Melleray and Roscrea in Ireland, Mount Saint Bernard in England and Gethsemani in the USA.
fact: «Trappist silence» means keeping very quiet.
fact: «TRAPPIST-1» is the name of a star about 40 light years away, so here the word is a label, not a monk.
exercise: «The Trappist monks prayed before dawn and then worked in the fields.» What does Trappist mean here? | *A member of a strict Catholic order of monks | A bright star in the night sky | A loud type of music | A famous footballer
exercise: «They kept a Trappist silence all morning.» Find and copy the word that means keeping quiet. | kept | morning | they | *silence
exercise: «They visited a Trappist monastery in Ireland.» What is a Trappist monastery? | A shop that sells bread and cakes | *A monastery connected with the strict Catholic order of Trappist monks | A school for young children | A river in the Irish hills
test: «The monks at the Trappist monastery farm the land and bake bread.» What does Trappist describe in this sentence? | *The strict Catholic order that the monastery belongs to | A type of star | A new school building | A kind of loud music
test: Which word names a monk who belongs to this strict order? | Abbey | *Trappist | Chapel | Brewer
exam: «TRAPPIST-1, a red dwarf about 40 light years away, has seven rocky planets.» In this sentence, what does TRAPPIST-1 mean? | A monk who prays in silence | *The name of a star, a small cool red star about 40 light years away | A brewery that makes Trappist beer | A recipe for bread
